{
	title: "A parent's message answers its subagent's question",
	spec: `Invariant: a subagent doing parent-delegated work can ask its parent for clarification without closing or deadlocking. A completed reply ending with <question> reaches the parent through the existing report path, wakes a parent waiting for a report under the normal delivery rules, and leaves the child open and waiting (autoclose, p87). The spawning parent answers through send with its default soft-steer delivery; that deliberate message starts the child again without requiring emergency or a human reply. Do not treat automatic reports, unrelated agent messages, or messages to a human-owned question as answers. Determine delegation ownership from the existing report-ownership rules, not merely the presence of a parent in session metadata. Human replies remain supported. Preserve question text, sender identity and normal attention rendering in web and terminal. Existing history and report machinery retain the question across restart; no new queue or polling loop. A completed non-question answer follows the existing reporting and autoclose rules, including untagged final answers.

Spawn guidance stays short: give the goal, constraints and expected result, not an exhaustive procedure. Ask the parent with <question> when missing information blocks the task; otherwise proceed. The parent answers from known requirements or asks its own user/parent when the decision is not its to make. Clarification neither allocates another spawn slot nor creates another session. Test the meaningful round trip: child question, parent receipt, normal parent answer, child continuation and final report; also preserve isolation from automatic reports and unrelated senders.`,
	status: 'planned',
